== Effects ==
* Makes all spikes retract, preventing them from dealing damage.
** Most spikes leave behind holes or a visual cue showing where they would normally be.
** The spikes around {{R|Curse Room}} doors are removed, allowing them to be entered and exited without taking damage.
** Retracts damaging spikes from [[Spiked Rock]]s and {{E|Spiked Chest}}s/{{E|Mimic Chest}}s.
** Removes the spikes from {{E|Poky|text=Pokies}}, {{E|Slide}}s, and {{E|Wall Hugger}}s.
*** Pokies, Slides, and Wall Huggers don't immediately stop moving once they are despiked, and are still able to push Isaac without dealing damage.
*** Has no effect on {{E|Grudge}}s, neither retracting their spikes nor despawning them.
** Causes {{E|Spikeball}}s to despawn.
*** Doesn't despawn or retract the spikes on {{E|Ball and Chain}}s.
*** Doesn't cause the moveable spike balls in {{E|Singe}}'s boss room to despawn or despike.

== Notes ==
* If Flat File is dropped in a room with spikes, the spikes will not extend again unless the room is left and re-entered.
** Spiked Rocks will not re-extend their spikes.
* {{E|Mimic Chest}}s won't change their contents when Isaac is up close to them (visible with {{i|Guppy's Eye}}) if opened under the effect of Flat File.
* Flat File also retracts the spikes in the center of {{R|Sacrifice Room}}s, making them unusable while the trinket is held. The spikes reappear after dropping the trinket and re-entering the room.
** If Flat File is gulped, Isaac cannot use Sacrifice rooms for the rest of the run.
* Flat File does not prevent {{E|The Pile}} or {{E|Mama Gurdy}} from using their spike attacks.
* Also removes spikes from doors in the [[Cursed!]] challenge, making it significantly easier.

== Interactions ==
* {{A|Golden Trinket|r+}} / {{I|Mom's Box|r+}}: Bosses spike attacks, {{E|Grudge}}, and {{E|Ball and Chain}} have their spikes retracted
* {{i|A Pound of Flesh}}: Doesn't retract spikes placed around consumables in shops.
* {{i|Sanguine Bond}}: Retracts the spikes, making the item useless.

